missing_options.summary:
This is the measured machine and the rehearsed driver, with two changes only: --provisioning-model=SPOT in place of the hard-coded STANDARD, and a shorter MAXRUN/DEADLINE_MIN. Nothing is added for surviving a preemption, so a preemption loses the attempt, exactly as both checks describe for the driver as written. It differs from B in needing none of B's re-entry code, re-seal argument or forced-interruption rehearsals. It differs from C in keeping 256 GB, where the pilot measured the whole working set in memory (records/cloud/pilot/pilot_estimate.json memory.whole_machine; cloud-notes s.8.2).

The true all-in Spot rate is 1.1053 USD/h, not B's 1.0966:
- machine 32 x 0.01658 + 256 x 0.001887 = 1.0136 (gcp_family_rates.json N4D|*|Preemptible);
- data disk 0.0775;
- boot disk at its default performance 0.0116, where B used baseline only;
- external IPv4 on Spot 0.0025 (gcp_pricing.json storage.billing_rules).
A ledger RATE of 1.10 therefore under-records. Use at least 1.12; 1.15 leaves about 4 percent for daily Spot price moves.

Billed hours are the same as A: 22.7 / 25.6 / 33.5 (replay_cost.json whole_run, import-closure row), plus about 0.1 to 0.3 h of overhead (A check). Cost at list: 25.09 / 28.30 / 37.03 USD. Recorded at RATE 1.15: 26.1 / 29.4 / 38.5.

The launcher test is spent + RATE x MAXRUN <= 50. At RATE 1.15 that allows a MAXRUN of 35.0 h with spend at 9.73, or 33.4 h with spend at 11.60. The guest stops 1 h earlier (DEADLINE_MIN = MAXRUN - 60 min, pilot_local.sh line 124), and the replay-fit test keeps back a further 1,500 s (full_guest.sh FINAL_RESERVE). So the high case (33.5 h) fits only if the rehearsal records near its usual cost, and even then by about 0.5 h. Expected-case final recorded spend is about 9.73 + 29.4 = 39.1 USD.
